r of each pool advanced to repêchage pools, with the winners of the repêchage pools earning bronze medals."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The two leading contenders were " [:a {:href "/athletes/34482"} "Detlef Ultsch"] " (GDR), the 1979 World Champion, and " [:a {:href "/athletes/33867"} "Aleksandrs Jackēvičs"] " from Latvia and the USSR. But Ultsch was defeated in his pool by Cuba’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/33439"} "Isaac Azcuy"] ". In the pool finals Jackēvičs faced the Swiss " [:a {:href "/athletes/34309"} "Jürg Röthlisberger"] ", who scored first with " [:em {} "koka"] " and avoided being thrown to hold on for the win. In the other pool, Azcuy was too much for Brazil’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/33556"} "Walter Carmona"] ". Ultsch and Jackēvičs went thru the repêchages with no difficulty and won bronze medals. In the final, Röthlisberger was immediately drawn into controversy about the size of his jacket. He was asked to change it but the referee then ruled that the second jacket was also not acceptable, so he went back to the first jacket, which was now allowed. Azcuy started the match quickly with three " [:em {} "kokas"] " using " [:em {} "sode-tsuri-komi-goshi"] ". But Röthlisberger answered with " [:em {} "harai-goshi"] " for " [:em {} "yuko"] " and won the gold medal. It was his second consecutive medal, having won bronze at half-heavyweight in Montréal."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/34309"} "Jürg Röthlisberger"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/SUI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/SUI.png"}] "SUI"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/33439"} "Isaac Azcuy"]] [:td {} [:a {:hr